\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Schematic illustration of the three observed deadlock mechanisms. The figure is conceptual (exact mid-run robot positions are not logged by the simulator); spatial relationships and arrows indicate the qualitative blocking structure that the run logs imply. \emph  {P1} (left): frequent low-trigger cycling on scattered storage chargers creates traffic on the same corridors as productive pod motion; mutual blocking arises because charging robots and pod-fetching robots compete for the same access paths. \emph  {P2} (centre): tight charge cycles with the interrupt disabled cause robots to occupy cluster cells for the full charging duration; cycles of mutual blocking form between cluster groups. \emph  {P3} (right): synchronisation resonance at $\tau _\text  {low}\approx 20\,\%$ causes near-simultaneous threshold crossings; the convergence wave on the picker-corridor cells is catastrophic because those cells double as productive-workflow cells.}}{19}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:deadlock_schematic}{{10}{19}{}{figure.10}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {IX}Limitations}{19}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:limitations}{{IX}{19}{}{section.9}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {X}Conclusion}{19}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:conclusion}{{X}{19}{}{section.10}{}}
\bibcite{kundu2023}{1}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces End-of-run battery distribution across the 20-robot fleet at $T = \SI {100000}{\second }$, $|C|=12$, one panel per placement pipeline. P3 and P4 exhibit a bimodal pattern with a heavy mass at $0\,\%$ (the 17/20 dead robots) and a small surviving subset at moderate state of charge; P1 and P2 are more dispersed with most of the fleet alive but at low battery (below $\tau _\text  {low}=20\,\%$). The pattern is consistent with the per-pipeline depletion mechanism analysis: scattered-charger placements (P1, P2) distribute charge access broadly but at low per-pass intensity, producing the spread; dwell-aligned (P3) and perimeter-isolated (P4) placements concentrate charge access either into a contested zone (P3) or behind a long round-trip (P4), producing the bimodal survival pattern.}}{20}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:depletion}{{11}{20}{}{figure.11}{}}
